note top of Order
  <b>Encapsulation of State and Pricing</b>
  • Private mutable fields (<i>status</i>, <i>completedPrepUnits</i>)
    can only transition via guarded domain methods:
    <i>advancePreparation()</i>, <i>markServed()</i>,
    <i>markPaid()</i>, and <i>markCancelled()</i>.
  • <i>finalPriceCents</i> is immutable and locked at order creation.
end note

note bottom of Customer
  <b>Polymorphic Customer Behaviour</b>
  • <i>applyTurnEndSatisfactionDecay()</i> calls
    <i>getWaitingSatisfactionLoss()</i> on the customer object.
  • Regular customers lose 8 points and pay full price.
  • VIP customers lose 5 points and receive 10% off.
  • Critics lose 12 points and choose the cheapest item.
  • Regular and VIP customers choose from all six menu items.
  • <i>recoverSatisfaction()</i> restores waiting customers
    by up to 15 points during Happy Hour, capped at 100.
end note

note top of Restaurant
  <b>Restaurant Composition</b>
  • <i>Restaurant</i> owns the lifecycle of its <i>Table</i>s,
    <i>WaitingQueue</i>, <i>Menu</i>, <i>GameConfig</i>, <i>Staff</i>, and <i>HappyHour</i>.
  • <i>createCustomer()</i> creates VIP C2, Critic C5,
    and Regular customers for the other arrivals.
  • Collections (<i>tables</i>, <i>orders</i>) and <i>WaitingQueue</i>
    expose unmodifiable views to prevent external mutation.
end note

note bottom of ComboMeal
  <b>Menu Abstraction and Shared Components</b>
  • <i>Dish</i> and <i>ComboMeal</i> implement <i>MenuItem</i>.
  • Each combo references two existing menu items.
  • Preparation units are summed. The price is 90% of the sum,
    rounded to the nearest cent. Components remain in the menu.
  • <i>Order</i> handles either implementation through <i>MenuItem</i>.
end note

note top of HappyHour
  <b>Encapsulated Promotion Policy</b>
  • Activation is available once per game and lasts two turns.
  • New orders receive 20% off after the VIP discount.
  • <i>Order.finalPriceCents</i> retains the price calculated
    when the order is placed.
  • <i>GameController</i> coordinates activation and turn expiry.
  • <i>Restaurant</i> applies recovery to waiting customers.
end note

